<title>UK: Trinkaus &amp; Burkhardt sets currency warrants.</title>
<headline>Trinkaus &amp; Burkhardt sets currency warrants.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trinkaus &amp; Burkhardt said it had issued 180 million call and put warrants, in 18 equal tranches, on the U.S. dollar/mark and yen/mark.</p>
<p>Twelve tranches are American-style currency warrants. There are five call warrant tranches and two put warant tranches on the U.S dollar/mark and there are three call warrant tranches and two put warrant tranches on the yen/mark.</p>
<p>There are also six European-style power warrants on the U.S. dollar/mark, three call and three put tranches. The exercise day is June 16, 1997.</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p> PAYDATE	   19.SEP.96		 MIN EXER LOT ONE</p>
<p> LISTING	   BERLIN, DUSS, FRFT, HAMBURG, STUTTGART</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
